{"page":106,"verses":[{"verse_key":"4:176","surah":4,"ayah":176,"ar_uthmani":"يَسْتَفْتُونَكَ قُلِ ٱللَّهُ يُفْتِيكُمْ فِى ٱلْكَلَـٰلَةِ ۚ إِنِ ٱمْرُؤٌا۟ هَلَكَ لَيْسَ لَهُۥ وَلَدٌ وَلَهُۥٓ أُخْتٌ فَلَهَا نِصْفُ مَا تَرَكَ ۚ وَهُوَ يَرِثُهَآ إِن لَّمْ يَكُن لَّهَا وَلَدٌ ۚ فَإِن كَانَتَا ٱثْنَتَيْنِ فَلَهُمَا ٱلثُّلُثَانِ مِمَّا تَرَكَ ۚ وَإِن كَانُوٓا۟ إِخْوَةً رِّجَالًا وَنِسَآءً فَلِلذَّكَرِ مِثْلُ حَظِّ ٱلْأُنثَيَيْنِ ۗ يُبَيِّنُ ٱللَّهُ لَكُمْ أَن تَضِلُّوا۟ ۗ وَٱللَّهُ بِكُلِّ شَىْءٍ عَلِيمٌۢ","en_translation_id":85,"en":"They ask you [Prophet] for a ruling. Say, ‘God gives you a ruling about inheritance from someone who dies childless with no surviving parents. If a man leaves a sister, she is entitled to half of the inheritance; if she has no child her brother is her sole heir; if there are two sisters, they are entitled to two-thirds of the inheritance between them, but if there are surviving brothers and sisters, the male is entitled to twice the share of the female. God makes this clear to you so that you do not make mistakes: He has full knowledge of everything.’","words":[{"pos":1,"ar":"يَسْتَفْتُونَكَ","en_gloss":"They seek your ruling","transliteration":"yastaftūnaka","verse_key":"4:176"},{"pos":2,"ar":"قُلِ","en_gloss":"Say","transliteration":"quli","verse_key":"4:176"},{"pos":3,"ar":"ٱللَّهُ","en_gloss":"Allah","transliteration":"l-lahu","verse_key":"4:176"},{"pos":4,"ar":"يُفْتِيكُمْ","en_gloss":"gives you a ruling","transliteration":"yuf'tīkum","verse_key":"4:176"},{"pos":5,"ar":"فِى","en_gloss":"concerning","transliteration":"fī","verse_key":"4:176"},{"pos":6,"ar":"ٱلْكَلَـٰلَةِ ۚ","en_gloss":"the Kalala","transliteration":"l-kalālati","verse_key":"4:176"},{"pos":7,"ar":"إِنِ","en_gloss":"if","transliteration":"ini","verse_key":"4:176"},{"pos":8,"ar":"ٱمْرُؤٌا۟","en_gloss":"a man","transliteration":"im'ru-on","verse_key":"4:176"},{"pos":9,"ar":"هَلَكَ","en_gloss":"died","transliteration":"halaka","verse_key":"4:176"},{"pos":10,"ar":"لَيْسَ","en_gloss":"(and) not","transliteration":"laysa","verse_key":"4:176"},{"pos":11,"ar":"لَهُۥ","en_gloss":"he has","transliteration":"lahu","verse_key":"4:176"},{"pos":12,"ar":"وَلَدٌۭ","en_gloss":"a child","transliteration":"waladun","verse_key":"4:176"},{"pos":13,"ar":"وَلَهُۥٓ","en_gloss":"and he has","transliteration":"walahu","verse_key":"4:176"},{"pos":14,"ar":"أُخْتٌۭ","en_gloss":"a sister","transliteration":"ukh'tun","verse_key":"4:176"},{"pos":15,"ar":"فَلَهَا","en_gloss":"then for her","transliteration":"falahā","verse_key":"4:176"},{"pos":16,"ar":"نِصْفُ","en_gloss":"(is) a half","transliteration":"niṣ'fu","verse_key":"4:176"},{"pos":17,"ar":"مَا","en_gloss":"(of) what","transliteration":"mā","verse_key":"4:176"},{"pos":18,"ar":"تَرَكَ ۚ","en_gloss":"he left","transliteration":"taraka","verse_key":"4:176"},{"pos":19,"ar":"وَهُوَ","en_gloss":"And he","transliteration":"wahuwa","verse_key":"4:176"},{"pos":20,"ar":"يَرِثُهَآ","en_gloss":"will inherit from her","transliteration":"yarithuhā","verse_key":"4:176"},{"pos":21,"ar":"إِن","en_gloss":"if","transliteration":"in","verse_key":"4:176"},{"pos":22,"ar":"لَّمْ","en_gloss":"not","transliteration":"lam","verse_key":"4:176"},{"pos":23,"ar":"يَكُن","en_gloss":"is","transliteration":"yakun","verse_key":"4:176"},{"pos":24,"ar":"لَّهَا","en_gloss":"for her","transliteration":"lahā","verse_key":"4:176"},{"pos":25,"ar":"وَلَدٌۭ ۚ","en_gloss":"a child","transliteration":"waladun","verse_key":"4:176"},{"pos":26,"ar":"فَإِن","en_gloss":"But if","transliteration":"fa-in","verse_key":"4:176"},{"pos":27,"ar":"كَانَتَا","en_gloss":"there were","transliteration":"kānatā","verse_key":"4:176"},{"pos":28,"ar":"ٱثْنَتَيْنِ","en_gloss":"two females","transliteration":"ith'natayni","verse_key":"4:176"},{"pos":29,"ar":"فَلَهُمَا","en_gloss":"then for them","transliteration":"falahumā","verse_key":"4:176"},{"pos":30,"ar":"ٱلثُّلُثَانِ","en_gloss":"two thirds","transliteration":"l-thuluthāni","verse_key":"4:176"},{"pos":31,"ar":"مِمَّا","en_gloss":"of what","transliteration":"mimmā","verse_key":"4:176"},{"pos":32,"ar":"تَرَكَ ۚ","en_gloss":"he left","transliteration":"taraka","verse_key":"4:176"},{"pos":33,"ar":"وَإِن","en_gloss":"But if","transliteration":"wa-in","verse_key":"4:176"},{"pos":34,"ar":"كَانُوٓا۟","en_gloss":"they were","transliteration":"kānū","verse_key":"4:176"},{"pos":35,"ar":"إِخْوَةًۭ","en_gloss":"brothers and sisters","transliteration":"ikh'watan","verse_key":"4:176"},{"pos":36,"ar":"رِّجَالًۭا","en_gloss":"men","transliteration":"rijālan","verse_key":"4:176"},{"pos":37,"ar":"وَنِسَآءًۭ","en_gloss":"and women","transliteration":"wanisāan","verse_key":"4:176"},{"pos":38,"ar":"فَلِلذَّكَرِ","en_gloss":"then the male will have","transliteration":"falildhakari","verse_key":"4:176"},{"pos":39,"ar":"مِثْلُ","en_gloss":"like","transliteration":"mith'lu","verse_key":"4:176"},{"pos":40,"ar":"حَظِّ","en_gloss":"share","transliteration":"ḥaẓẓi","verse_key":"4:176"},{"pos":41,"ar":"ٱلْأُنثَيَيْنِ ۗ","en_gloss":"(of) the two females","transliteration":"l-unthayayni","verse_key":"4:176"},{"pos":42,"ar":"يُبَيِّنُ","en_gloss":"makes clear","transliteration":"yubayyinu","verse_key":"4:176"},{"pos":43,"ar":"ٱللَّهُ","en_gloss":"Allah","transliteration":"l-lahu","verse_key":"4:176"},{"pos":44,"ar":"لَكُمْ","en_gloss":"to you","transliteration":"lakum","verse_key":"4:176"},{"pos":45,"ar":"أَن","en_gloss":"lest","transliteration":"an","verse_key":"4:176"},{"pos":46,"ar":"تَضِلُّوا۟ ۗ","en_gloss":"you go astray","transliteration":"taḍillū","verse_key":"4:176"},{"pos":47,"ar":"وَٱللَّهُ","en_gloss":"And Allah","transliteration":"wal-lahu","verse_key":"4:176"},{"pos":48,"ar":"بِكُلِّ","en_gloss":"of every","transliteration":"bikulli","verse_key":"4:176"},{"pos":49,"ar":"شَىْءٍ","en_gloss":"thing","transliteration":"shayin","verse_key":"4:176"},{"pos":50,"ar":"عَلِيمٌۢ","en_gloss":"(is) All-Knower","transliteration":"ʿalīmun","verse_key":"4:176"},{"pos":51,"ar":"١٧٦","en_gloss":"(176)","transliteration":"","verse_key":"4:176"}]},{"verse_key":"5:1","surah":5,"ayah":1,"ar_uthmani":" يَـٰٓأَيُّهَا ٱلَّذِينَ ءَامَنُوٓا۟ أَوْفُوا۟ بِٱلْعُقُودِ ۚ أُحِلَّتْ لَكُم بَهِيمَةُ ٱلْأَنْعَـٰمِ إِلَّا مَا يُتْلَىٰ عَلَيْكُمْ غَيْرَ مُحِلِّى ٱلصَّيْدِ وَأَنتُمْ حُرُمٌ ۗ إِنَّ ٱللَّهَ يَحْكُمُ مَا يُرِيدُ","en_translation_id":85,"en":"You who believe, fulfil your obligations. Livestock animals are lawful as food for you, with the exception of what is about to be announced to you. You are forbidden to kill game while you are on pilgrimage––God commands what He will,","words":[{"pos":1,"ar":"يَـٰٓأَيُّهَا","en_gloss":"O","transliteration":"yāayyuhā","verse_key":"5:1"},{"pos":2,"ar":"ٱلَّذِينَ","en_gloss":"you (who)","transliteration":"alladhīna","verse_key":"5:1"},{"pos":3,"ar":"ءَامَنُوٓا۟","en_gloss":"believe","transliteration":"āmanū","verse_key":"5:1"},{"pos":4,"ar":"أَوْفُوا۟","en_gloss":"Fulfil","transliteration":"awfū","verse_key":"5:1"},{"pos":5,"ar":"بِٱلْعُقُودِ ۚ","en_gloss":"the contracts","transliteration":"bil-ʿuqūdi","verse_key":"5:1"},{"pos":6,"ar":"أُحِلَّتْ","en_gloss":"Are made lawful","transliteration":"uḥillat","verse_key":"5:1"},{"pos":7,"ar":"لَكُم","en_gloss":"for you","transliteration":"lakum","verse_key":"5:1"},{"pos":8,"ar":"بَهِيمَةُ","en_gloss":"the quadruped","transliteration":"bahīmatu","verse_key":"5:1"},{"pos":9,"ar":"ٱلْأَنْعَـٰمِ","en_gloss":"(of) the grazing livestock","transliteration":"l-anʿāmi","verse_key":"5:1"},{"pos":10,"ar":"إِلَّا","en_gloss":"except","transliteration":"illā","verse_key":"5:1"},{"pos":11,"ar":"مَا","en_gloss":"what","transliteration":"mā","verse_key":"5:1"},{"pos":12,"ar":"يُتْلَىٰ","en_gloss":"is recited","transliteration":"yut'lā","verse_key":"5:1"},{"pos":13,"ar":"عَلَيْكُمْ","en_gloss":"on you","transliteration":"ʿalaykum","verse_key":"5:1"},{"pos":14,"ar":"غَيْرَ","en_gloss":"not","transliteration":"ghayra","verse_key":"5:1"},{"pos":15,"ar":"مُحِلِّى","en_gloss":"being permitted","transliteration":"muḥillī","verse